      "message": "Do we actually compile `charge_state.c` in the QC case? If it is disabled for these boards, there should not be a conflict for `led_pwr_get_state()` or `charge_manager_get_active_charge_port()`. If there is no conflict, we don\u0027t need to touch `charge_state.c` to make these functions weak.\n\nSetting up a new subsystem to hold two variables feels like overkill. Also, calling it a virtual charge_state is a bit of an overstatement as it doesn\u0027t provide major charge_state functionalities.\n\nAs we have a dedicated ADSP comm module, it might be cleaner to just define these `led_pwr_get_state()` functions directly inside `adsp_comms.c`. That way, the module that owns the data provides the state directly.",
